<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92171" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥάξ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥᾱγός, ἡ</span>, 
			Ion.
		 and later Gr. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥώξ</span></b> 
		(v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥώξ</span> (B)):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>grape</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				398
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ ῥᾶγα βοτρύων</span> for
			each <i>grape</i> in the bunch, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				845a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥᾶγες βότρυος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					550a28
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pr.</u>
				925b15
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν αὐτῷ τῷ βότρυϊ ῥᾶγας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>CP</u>
					5.5.1
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1.21.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>HP</u>
				3.17.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς σταφυλὰς καὶ ὡς κατὰ μίαν αἱ
					ῥᾶγες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>Im.</u>
					1.31
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>berry</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				4.51
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥ. γλυκυσίδης</span>
			<i>seed</i> of peony, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Eup.</u>
				2.117
			</span></i>; <i>clove</i> of garlic, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.152
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>a venomous kind of spider, malmignatte</i>, so called from its
			shape, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				3.36
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> pl.,
				<i>finger-tips</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
				<u>Onom.</u>
				85
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.146
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥάξ</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θηλή</span>
			, 'in common speech', <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1485.59
			</span></i>. [In <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				184
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥα̈́γεσσι</span> should be read
			for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥᾰγέεσσι</span>.]</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
